From 18e0331690654f2323d94fb7a0f6e0c8c00d3a93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:55:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] input: tpkit/parade: an empty input buffer is not an error

With the screen on, ts_kit's ESD watchdog sends the touch IC a PIP NULL
command every second. The level-low interrupt is unmasked right after
the response is read while the IC is still releasing INT, so it fires
once more and that read finds the 2-byte empty buffer. Huawei's driver
logged this normal PIP condition at error level, filling the kernel log
with "parade_read_input: input_buf is empty" once a second. Log it at
ts_kit's debug level, as Parade's reference driver treats it; the read
is still skipped as before. Stock configures the same watchdog and IRQ.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016iwHzV2tPonTxdceSkWZtS
---
 drivers/devkit/tpkit/panel/parade/parade.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/devkit/tpkit/panel/parade/parade.c b/drivers/devkit/tpkit/panel/parade/parade.c
index 39ecccc6..14d50ea8 100644
--- a/drivers/devkit/tpkit/panel/parade/parade.c
+++ b/drivers/devkit/tpkit/panel/parade/parade.c
@@ -5850,8 +5850,12 @@ if (rc < 0) {
 		return 0;
 	if (size == 2 || size > CY_MAX_INPUT){
 		/* Before PIP 1.7, empty buffer is 0x0002;
-		From PIP 1.7, empty buffer is 0xFFXX */
-		TS_LOG_ERR("%s: input_buf is empty, inval size=%d\n",__func__,size);
+		From PIP 1.7, empty buffer is 0xFFXX.
+		An empty buffer is normal: the level-low interrupt is unmasked right
+		after a response is read, while the IC is still releasing INT, so every
+		ESD watchdog ping (once a second with the screen on) is followed by one
+		empty read. Log it at debug level, as Parade's reference driver does. */
+		TS_LOG_DEBUG("%s: input_buf is empty, size=%d\n",__func__,size);
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 	rc = cd->parade_chip_data->ts_platform_data->bops->bus_read(&reg_addr, sizeof(reg_addr), cd->input_buf, size);
-- 
